      "Engagement letters go stale. The client adds a second GSTIN, converts to a private limited company or starts exporting, and the original scope no longer describes the work. Review letters annually, ideally at the start of each financial year, and whenever the client's structure changes.",
      "Store signed letters in the client's record alongside the engagement itself, so anyone working on the client can see what was agreed. In ClientSpace, engagement scope sits with the client's tasks and fixed-fee tracking, and clients can approve documents through the portal, which keeps the letter, the work and the effort data together. A letter in a filing cabinet that nobody reads protects no one.",
